/-!
# Genuine finite crossed braided gauging

An actual grading is given by actual natural orthogonal degree projectors,
with total, unit and tensor convolution equations. Their kernel images
give the actual complete homogeneous biproduct decomposition.
Alternatively, actual additive and retract-closed component properties,
with a unique component for each actual simple and actual tensor closure,
construct these projectors and the tensor convolution equation. An actual
component-permuting action then gives their actual conjugation equation.

An actual weak monoidal action conjugates these projectors. Actual
homogeneous crossed isomorphisms, natural in both variables and satisfying
the crossed unit, two hexagon and weak-action equivariance equations,
produce an actual braiding on the equivariantization. Its finite simple
skeleton, dual pairings and simple unit are actual constructed structures.

Faithfulness of the actual grading and nondegeneracy of the actual braided
neutral full category imply actual Müger nondegeneracy of gauging. The
proof uses the actual regular unit object to detect degrees, genuine
induction dominance, and faithful tensoring to recover equivariant unit
maps. There is no ordinary braiding or pivotal structure on the entire
graded category among the assumptions.

This construction is not an existence theorem for a crossed extension of
an arbitrary categorical action. Such existence still requires actual
Picard component products and an actual crossed realization instantiating
the structural inputs above.
-/
